-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/f5172b32-6d46-52d3-a164-faecd36f5f1e
-- title:
--   Twisted elliptic transfer identity for one norm class
-- statement:
--   Fix number fields $K$ and $L$ with $L/K$ a Galois extension of finite degree, and write $\mathbb{A}_K =$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K`, $\mathbb{A}_L =$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 L) L`, and `AdelicGL2` for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the respective adele ring. The hypothesis `hprime` asserts that $[L:K] =$ `Module.finrank K L` is prime. Real numbers $\alpha,\beta$ are given with $0 < \alpha$ (`hα`) and $\alpha < \beta$ (`hαβ`); the set $\{g \mid \mathrm{ideleNorm}(\det g) \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$, where [`NumberField.TateGlobal.ideleNorm F x`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L19) is the modulus of the Haar character of $x$ acting on $\mathbb{A}_F$, is referred to below as the slab. The idele unit groups $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ and $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ carry their Borel structures, and $\nu_{Z_L}$, $\nu_{Z_K}$ are Haar measures on them. A datum $D$ of type [`M4aHerbrand.IdeleGaloisDescent (𝓞 L) K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_IdeleClassVocab.html#L28) is given, that is, a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ which is compatible with the diagonal embedding of $L$ and continuous in each automorphism; [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ.symm`](def/AutomorphicForm_SigmaAdelicAction.html#L14) denotes the induced automorphism of `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 L) L` obtained by applying `D.act σ.symm` entrywise. An element $\sigma$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ is given with $\sigma \neq 1$ (`hσ`) and such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma^{-1}$ (`hgen`).
--
--   Characters: $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ whose associated $\mathbb{C}$-valued function is continuous (`hξc`) and which is trivial on the image of $L^\times$ (`hξt`). A finite set $\Xi$ of homomorphisms from the full subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ is given, and `hΞ` characterises membership in $\Xi$: a character $\xi$ belongs to $\Xi$ exactly when it is continuous as a $\mathbb{C}$-valued function, trivial on the image of $K^\times$, and satisfies $\xi \circ N = \xi_L$, where $N =$ `(M4aHerbrand.GenuineDescent.genuineBaseChange K L).idelicNorm` is the map $\mathbb{A}_L^\times \to \mathbb{A}_K^\times$ induced by the algebra norm for the base-change homomorphism $\mathbb{A}_K \to \mathbb{A}_L$.
--
--   Representatives and fundamental domains. A set $R_L \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ is contained (`hRLsub`) in the set of those $\delta$ whose $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted conjugacy class has [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766)-image equal to the conjugacy class of some $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ lying in [`AutomorphicForm.ellipticCell K`](def/AutomorphicForm_GL2ConjugacyCells.html#L35) (the characteristic polynomial of $\gamma$ has no root in $K$) or in [`AutomorphicForm.centralCell K`](def/AutomorphicForm_GL2ConjugacyCells.html#L26) (the matrix of $\gamma$ is a scalar multiple of the identity); and `hRL` asserts that every $\delta$ in that set has a unique $\delta_0 \in R_L$ with $\delta = \mathrm{scalar}(u)\,(h^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(h))$ for some $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $u \in L^\times$. A family $\Psi_L$ of subsets of `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 L) L` satisfies: for each $\delta_0 \in R_L$, $\Psi_L(\delta_0)$ lies in the slab (`hΨLs`) and is a fundamental domain (`hΨL`) for the image under [`AutomorphicForm.globalPoints (𝓞 L) L`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L15) of the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted centraliser $\{t \mid t\,\delta_0\,\sigma^{-1}(t)^{-1} = \delta_0\}$ of $\delta_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, for the adelic Haar measure `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L` restricted to the slab. A set $\Theta \subseteq \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ is a fundamental domain for $\nu_{Z_L}$ and the range of the homomorphism $L^\times \to \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ given by $u \mapsto \sigma^{-1}(u)u^{-1}$ followed by the embedding of $L^\times$ (`hΘ`). Likewise a set $R_K \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ is contained in the union of the central and elliptic cells (`hRKsub`), `hRK` asserts that every $\gamma$ in that union has a unique $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ with $\gamma = \mathrm{scalar}(a')(h^{-1}\gamma_0 h)$ for some $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, $a' \in K^\times$, and the family $\Psi_K$ satisfies, for each $\gamma_0 \in R_K$, that $\Psi_K(\gamma_0)$ lies in the slab (`hΨKs`) and is a fundamental domain (`hΨK`) for the image under [`AutomorphicForm.globalPoints (𝓞 K) K`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L15) of the centraliser of $\gamma_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, with respect to `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 K) K` restricted to the slab.
--
--   Constants and transfer hypotheses. A constant $c_0 \in \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ and a real $\kappa > 0$ (`hκ`) are given such that integration over $\Theta$ against $\nu_{Z_L}$ of a function pulled back along $N$ equals $\kappa$ times integration over the range of $N$ against $\nu_{Z_K}$: `hκl` states this for lower integrals of measurable $\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^\infty$-valued functions with factor `ENNReal.ofReal κ`, and `hκi` states, for measurable $\mathbb{C}$-valued $g$, both the equivalence of integrability of $g \circ N$ on $\Theta$ for $\nu_{Z_L}$ with integrability of $g$ on the range of $N$ for $\nu_{Z_K}$, and the corresponding equality of integrals with factor $\kappa$. Test functions $\varphi$ on `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 L) L` and $f$ on `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 K) K` are continuous with compact support (`hφ`, `hφc`, `hf`, `hfc`). The hypothesis `hOn` states [`AutomorphicForm.AreMatchingOn K L (AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K) σ.symm`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L324) for: the pushforward of `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L` along the entrywise map induced by the inverse of the ring isomorphism $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \cong \mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ built from `Algebra.TensorProduct.comm` and [`M4aHerbrand.Bridge.genuineRingEquiv`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineTensorEquiv.html#L57); the measure $c_0 \cdot$ `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 K) K`; the function $\varphi$ transported along the forward isomorphism; and $f$. Unfolded, this is the conjunction of two clauses: first, for all $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ whose norm string $\prod_{i<[L:K]} \sigma^{-i}(\delta)$ is regular semisimple (its $\mathrm{tr}^2 - 4\det$ is a unit), all regular semisimple $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, all $y$ with $\gamma$ (pushed into $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$) equal to $y^{-1}$ times the norm string of $\delta$ times $y$, and all Haar measures on the centraliser of $\gamma$ and on the twisted centraliser of $\delta$ which are coupled via conjugation by $y$, every twisted orbital integral of the transported $\varphi$ at $\delta$ equals every orbital integral of $f$ at $\gamma$; second, for every regular semisimple $\gamma$ that is not a twisted norm of any $\delta$, every orbital integral of $f$ at $\gamma$ with respect to a Haar measure on the centraliser of $\gamma$ vanishes. Here an orbital integral of $f$ at $\gamma$ with value $I$ means that there is a nonnegative measurable compactly supported weight $w$ whose integral $\int w(tx)\,d\tau$ over the centraliser equals $1$ whenever $f(x^{-1}\gamma x) \neq 0$, and $I = \int f(x^{-1}\gamma x)w(x)\,d\mu$.
--
--   The vanishing hypothesis `hvan` requires: for every $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ lying in the elliptic cell, every $a' \in K^\times$ and every $u \in \mathbb{A}_K^\times$ such that the conjugacy class of $\mathrm{scalar}(a')\gamma_0$ is not in the range of [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766), and such that there exists $c \in (L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ with norm string of $\mathrm{scalar}(c)$ equal to the image of the central scalar $u$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, every orbital integral of $f$ at the element `globalPoints (𝓞 K) K γ₀` $\cdot$ `centralScalar (𝓞 K) K` $(a'u)$, with respect to $c_0 \cdot$ `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 K) K` and any Haar measure on the centraliser of that element, is $0$.
--
--   Finally, $\delta_0 \in R_L$, $\gamma_0 \in R_K$ with $\gamma_0$ in the elliptic cell, and $a \in K^\times$ are given such that `normClassMap hgen` sends the $\sigma^{-1}$-twisted conjugacy class of $\delta_0$ to the conjugacy class of $\mathrm{scalar}(a)\gamma_0$ (`hNcl`).
--
--   The conclusion is the single identity
--   $$\int_{\Theta} \xi_L(z)\Bigl(\int_{\Psi_L(\delta_0)} \varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\,\delta_0\,\sigma_D^{-1}(\mathrm{scalar}(z)\,x)\bigr)\,dx\Bigr)\,d\nu_{Z_L}(z) = \frac{c_0\,\kappa}{[L:K]\cdot\max(1,|\Xi|)}\sum_{\xi_K \in \Xi} \int_{N(\mathbb{A}_L^\times)} \xi_K(a u)\Bigl(\int_{\Psi_K(\gamma_0)} f\bigl(x^{-1}\,\gamma_0\,(\mathrm{scalar}(a u)\,x)\bigr)\,dx\Bigr)\,d\nu_{Z_K}(u),$$
--   where on the left $\delta_0$ and on the right $\gamma_0$ stand for their images under `globalPoints`, $\mathrm{scalar}$ for `centralScalar`, $\sigma_D^{-1}$ for [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaAdelicAct K L D σ.symm`](def/AutomorphicForm_SigmaAdelicAction.html#L14), the inner integrals are against the respective adelic Haar measures `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L` and `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 K) K`, $a$ denotes the principal idele attached to $a \in K^\times$, the domain of the outer integral on the right is the range of $N$, and the scalar prefactor is the real number $(c_0\kappa)/([L:K]\cdot\max(1,|\Xi|))$ viewed in $\mathbb{C}$, with $|\Xi|$ the cardinality of the finite set $\Xi$.
--
--   This is the class-by-class elliptic transfer step in the comparison of the $\sigma$-twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over $L$ with the trace formula over $K$, in the style of Langlands' base change for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$: it converts the twisted elliptic term attached to one representative $\delta_0$ into the sum over the characters $\xi_K \in \Xi$ of the corresponding untwisted elliptic terms at the matched class $a\gamma_0$. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.finsum_sigmaCentralizerDomain_ellipticNorm_eq_mul_sum_finsum_centralizerDomain_elliptic_of_areMatchingOn_of_eq_zero`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.finsum_sigmaCentralizerDomain_ellipticNorm_eq_mul_sum_finsum_centralizerDomain_elliptic_of_areMatchingOn_of_eq_zero), which sums these per-class identities over the representatives.
